  "experiment": {
    "claim": "Issue #495 -- NOT a spec claim (spec/target-spec.md has no ratified POR_RAW-glitch, ramp or reset row as of this record). Replaces the mismatch-seed reproduction of the ss/-40C mc14 pulse (PR #491 replay-474) with a deterministic forced offset: a DC source VOFF in series with the gate of XMOL2 (the output leg of the OK detector's XMOL1/XMOL2 mirror) in a DERIVED copy of design/netlist/bias_core.spice, swept over -12..+12 mV, so the early-assertion / pulse behaviour has a repeatable testbench that does not depend on a mismatch seed. Every point is nominal-process (no _mm section): the offset is the only variation. Records, per point: the VDD at which BIAS_OK first asserts, every POR_RAW high interval on the UP segment other than the genuine release (pulse start/end VDD, width in volts and measured seconds), the genuine VPOR-up, and whether RESETn (real por_output_chain on the shared IBIAS) is released by a pulse. Each point is run under the default start, `uic`, and `gmin=1e-11` so solver-state dependence is stated, not assumed. Design and spec are unchanged.",
    "provenance": "schematic",
    "provenance_source": "sim/por-bias-ok-early-assert/testbench/tb_bias_ok_early_assert.sch",
    "slug": "por-bias-ok-early-assert",
    "statistical_convention": "N/A (deterministic forced-offset sweep of the nominal drawn circuit, not a distribution claim). The offset axis is a sensitivity sweep; sigma_XMOL ~2.9 mV (issue #455) is used only to label +-3 sigma ~ +-9 mV input-referred.",
    "title": "Deterministic forced-offset reproduction of the early BIAS_OK assertion / POR_RAW release-then-reassert pulse (bias_core OK detector, real por_comparator + por_output_chain)"
  },
